{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1780723395973,"sessionID":"ses_1649db034ffe5PYzRZZZhfwsIg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"toolu_vrtx_01YTZLH9hC8H3VtCuBvc4QLA","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/reading-advantage-monorepo/measure/tracks/audit_log_retention_dsar_20260605/plan.md"},"output":"<path>/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/reading-advantage-monorepo/measure/tracks/audit_log_retention_dsar_20260605/plan.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Plan: Audit Log Retention + DSAR Bulk Export\n2: \n3: > Contract-First + TDD. Each phase ends with a verification step. Builds on the committed\n4: > `audit_events` table and `recordAuditEvent` helper. Runtime tests use the real\n5: > `science_advantage_test` DB (append-only DELETE cannot be exercised against mock-db).\n6: \n7: ## Phase 0: Setup\n8: - [ ] Task: Confirm `packages/db/src/schema/audit.ts` and `packages/auth/src/audit.ts` are present at HEAD (committed `87b2432`); read both to capture the exact `auditEvents` columns and `recordAuditEvent` signature.\n9: - [ ] Task: Locate the privileged/DDL connection used by `drizzle-kit migrate` (`DIRECT_DATABASE_URL`); confirm it has DELETE on `audit_events` (the app role does not).\n10: - [ ] Task: Read `lib/platform/session-cleanup.ts` to reuse the periodic-job + advisory-lock pattern.\n11: \n12: ## Phase 1: Retention Config (Contract)\n13: - [ ] Task: Add `AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS` to the validated env schema (`lib/env.ts` / shared env), default `2557`, `.refine(n => Number.isInteger(n) && n >= 365)`.\n14: - [ ] Task: Write test asserting the default and that values < 365 throw at parse time.\n15: - [ ] Task: Document the policy in `packages/auth/README.md` + new `docs/compliance/retention.md`.\n16: - [ ] Task: Verify — env parse test passes.\n17: \n18: ## Phase 2: Purge Function (TDD)\n19: - [ ] Task: Write `audit-retention.test.ts` (integration): seed rows at `window-1d` (kept) and `window+1d` (purged); assert `purgeExpiredAuditEvents` deletes only the expired row and returns the count.\n20: - [ ] Task: Write test: purge runs in batches (`LIMIT 5000`) and loops until empty (seed > 5000 expired rows or stub the batch size).\n21: - [ ] Task: Write test: a successful purge records exactly one `audit:retention_purge` event with the deleted count.\n22: - [ ] Task: Implement `packages/auth/src/audit-retention.ts` `purgeExpiredAuditEvents(now)` using the privileged connection + batched DELETE + post-purge `recordAuditEvent`.\n23: - [ ] Task: Export from `packages/auth/src/index.ts`.\n24: - [ ] Task: Verify — `pnpm turbo run test --filter=@reading-advantage/auth` green.\n25: \n26: ## Phase 3: Periodic Job\n27: - [ ] Task: Write test: concurrent invocation is guarded by `pg_try_advisory_lock` (second caller no-ops).\n28: - [ ] Task: Add the scheduler entry (mirror `session-cleanup.ts`): daily at a low-traffic hour, wrapped in the advisory lock.\n29: - [ ] Task: Verify — advisory-lock test green; job registers without throwing on boot.\n30: \n31: ## Phase 4: DSAR Domain Function (TDD)\n32: - [ ] Task: Add `dsar:export` permission key to `packages/auth`; update `assertCan` coverage test.\n33: - [ ] Task: Write `dsar.test.ts` (integration): two-school fixture; assert `exportSubjectData` returns the subject's profile + audit events + activity, and that an admin in school A is DENIED a subject in school B.\n34: - [ ] Task: Write test: export streams/paginates and returns `tooLarge` when the row ceiling is exceeded.\n35: - [ ] Task: Implement `packages/domain/src/audit/dsar.ts` `exportSubjectData(tenant, subjectRef)` via `createTenantDB`, gated by `assertCan(actor, 'dsar:export')`, paginated reads, row ceiling.\n36: - [ ] Task: Verify — domain DSAR tests green; `tenant-coverage.test.ts` still passes (function uses `createTenantDB`).\n37: \n38: ## Phase 5: DSAR Endpoint (TDD)\n39: - [ ] Task: Write route test: ADMIN-only (non-admin → 403); Zod rejects neither/both of `userId`/`email`; valid request re