re/tracks/audit_log_retention_dsar_20260605/plan.md","time":{"start":1780723395912,"end":1780723395948}},"id":"prt_e9b62ad22001fOkIcgx5j64GNU","sessionID":"ses_1649db034ffe5PYzRZZZhfwsIg","messageID":"msg_e9b6292e9001Zr01gInx7VdxvR"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1780723395973,"sessionID":"ses_1649db034ffe5PYzRZZZhfwsIg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"toolu_vrtx_01U5yE22UfEqLMi3crwwzgVw","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/reading-advantage-monorepo/measure/tracks/audit_log_retention_dsar_20260605/spec.md"},"output":"<path>/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/reading-advantage-monorepo/measure/tracks/audit_log_retention_dsar_20260605/spec.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Specification: Audit Log Retention + DSAR Bulk Export\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: \n5: Two compliance capabilities that sit directly on top of the append-only `audit_events`\n6: table delivered by `audit_log_infrastructure_20260603`:\n7: \n8: 1. **Retention** — a 7-year (FERPA) retention window with a periodic, idempotent cleanup\n9:    job that deletes `audit_events` rows older than the window. Append-only `REVOKE\n10:    UPDATE, DELETE` means the cleanup job must run as a privileged role; the deletion path\n11:    is the *only* sanctioned mutation and is itself audited.\n12: 2. **DSAR bulk export** — a GDPR/FERPA Data Subject Access Request endpoint that, given a\n13:    subject (user id or email), gathers all audit events and profile/activity records for\n14:    that subject into a single downloadable archive (JSON + a human-readable manifest),\n15:    ADMIN-only and tenant-scoped.\n16: \n17: ## Problem\n18: \n19: District procurement and GDPR/FERPA compliance require both (a) a defensible data\n20: lifecycle (data is not kept forever) and (b) the ability to answer \"what do you hold\n21: about this person, and prove it.\" The audit-log track established the *write* side; this\n22: track establishes the *lifecycle* and *read-out* sides. Without retention, `audit_events`\n23: grows unbounded and violates data-minimization principles. Without DSAR export, the\n24: organization cannot satisfy a subject access request within the statutory window.\n25: \n26: ## Why\n27: \n28: - **FERPA**: education records have a defined retention obligation; 7 years is the policy\n29:   chosen for this monorepo (configurable via env).\n30: - **GDPR Art. 15 (right of access) + Art. 17 (right to erasure)**: a subject can request\n31:   a copy of their data and, separately, deletion. This track delivers Art. 15 (access)\n32:   and the retention half of Art. 17 (time-bounded deletion); subject-initiated erasure is\n33:   out of scope (see below).\n34: - Builds entirely on already-committed infrastructure (`audit_events`,\n35:   `recordAuditEvent`, the ADMIN-only `/api/admin/audit-events` pattern).\n36: \n37: ## Functional Requirements\n38: \n39: ### FR-1: Retention Policy Configuration\n40: - Add `AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS` to the validated env surface (default `2557` ≈ 7 years).\n41: - Add a `.refine` rule: must be a positive integer ≥ 365 (refuse footgun short windows).\n42: - Document the policy in `packages/auth/README.md` and a new\n43:   `docs/compliance/retention.md`.\n44: \n45: ### FR-2: Privileged Cleanup Path\n46: - Because `audit_events` has `REVOKE UPDATE, DELETE` for the app role, deletion must run\n47:   under a dedicated migration/maintenance role (the same role that owns DDL).\n48: - Add `packages/auth/src/audit-retention.ts` exporting\n49:   `purgeExpiredAuditEvents(now = new Date()): Promise<{ deleted: number }>` that issues a\n50:   batched `DELETE ... WHERE created_at < now() - interval` with `LIMIT 5000` per batch,\n51:   looping until no rows remain, using a direct (non-pooled, privileged) connection.\n52: - The purge run itself records an `audit:retention_purge` event (count, window, actor =\n53:   `system`) **after** the batch completes, via `recordAuditEvent`.\n54: \n55: ### FR-3: Periodic Cleanup Job\n56: - Add a scheduler entry (mirror `lib/platform/session-cleanup.ts`) that runs\n57:   `purgeExpiredAuditEvents` daily at a low-traffic hour.\n58: - Idempotent; safe to run concurrently (advisory lock via `pg_try_advisory_lock` so two\n59:   replicas don't double-run).\n60: \n61: ### FR-4: DSAR Export Domain Function\n62: - Add `packages/domain/src/audit/dsar.ts` (or extend `packages/domain/src/audit/`)\n63:   exporting `exportSubjectData(tenant, subjectRef): Promise<DsarBundle>` where\n64:   `subjectRef = { userId } | { email }`.\n65: - `DsarBundle` collects: the user profile, all `audit_events` where the subject is actor\n66:   or target, and the subject's activity/progress rows (scoped to the science-advantage\n67:   domain modules already migrated). Tenant-scoped via `createTenantDB`.\n68: - Guarded by `assertCan(actor, 'audit:read:all')` (the permission added in commit\n69:   `5eb0171`) plus an explicit `dsar:export` permission key (add to `packages/auth`).\n70: \n71: ### FR-5: DSAR Export Endpoint\n72: - Add `GET /api/admin/dsar/export?userId=...` (or `?email=...`), ADMIN-only, Zod-validated\n73:   query (exactly one of `userId`/`email`).\n74: - Returns `application/zip` (or `application/json` with `?format=json`) containing\n75:   `manifest.md` (human-readable summary: who, when, what categories, counts) +\n76:   `audit-events.json` + `profile.json` + `activity.json`.\n77: - The export action is itself audited as `dsar:export` (actor = requesting admin,\n78:   target = subject).\n79: \n80: ### FR-6: Rate + Size Guards\n81: - DSAR export is bounded: stream/paginate `audit_events` (do not load all rows into\n82:   memory); cap a single export at a configurable row ceiling and return `413` with a\n83:   guidance message if exceeded (operator can raise the ceiling).\n84: \n85: ## Non-Functional Requirements\n86: - The cleanup job must never delete rows inside the retention window (off-by-one and\n87:   timezone correctness covered by tests at the boundary).\n88: - Export must be tenant-isolated: an admin in school A cannot export a subject in school B.\n89: - `pnpm turbo run {test,build,check-types} --filter=@reading-advantage/auth\n90:   --filter=@reading-advantage/domain --filter=science-advantage` exits 0.\n91: \n92: ## Acceptance Criteria\n93: 1. `AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS` is validated env (default 2557; `.refine` ≥ 365).\n94: 2. `purgeExpiredAuditEvents` deletes only rows older than the window, in batches, under a\n95:    privileged connection, and records an `audit:retention_purge` event.\n96: 3. Daily scheduled job runs the purge under an advisory lock.\n97: 4. `exportSubjectData(tenant, subjectRef)` returns a tenant-scoped bundle gated by\n98:    `assertCan(... 'dsar:export')`.\n99: 5. `GET /api/admin/dsar/export` returns a zip/JSON archive; ADMIN-only; Zod-validated.\n100: 6. The export action is audited as `dsar:export`.\n101: 7. Tests: boundary retention (row at window-1 day kept, window+1 day purged); advisory\n102:    lock prevents concurrent double-run; cross-tenant export denied; export-too-large\n103:    returns 413; export bundle round-trips (manifest counts == file counts).\n104: 8. Quality gates green (test/build/check-types) for the four filtered packages/app.\n105: \n106: ## Out of Scope\n107: - **Subject-initiated erasure** (GDPR Art. 17 \"right to be forgotten\" on demand) — audit\n108:   events are append-only and legally retained; erasure of *profile* data is a separate\n109:   track with its own legal-hold rules.\n110: - **Real-time audit-event streaming** to a SIEM — soft-depends on\n111:   `observability_stack_20260603`; this track is batch-only.\n112: - Retention for tables other than `audit_events` (sessions, login_attempts have their own\n113:   cleanup) — separate, already-tracked.\n114: - A UI for DSAR export — endpoint only; admin console wiring is a follow-up.\n115: \n116: ## Constraints & Risks\n117: - **Risk: running DELETE against an append-only table.** Mitigation: the privileged\n118:   connection is the *only* path; it is exercised exclusively by the purge function, which\n119:   is itself audited. Document the role separation.\n120: - **Risk: DSAR export is a PII egress point.** Mitigation: ADMIN-only, tenant-scoped,\n121:   audited, size-capped, and uses the same `safeMetadata` redaction posture for any nested\n122:   metadata that should not leave the system.\n123: - **Risk: timezone/off-by-one in retention boundary.** Mitigation: store + compare in UTC\n124:   (`withTimezone: true`); explicit boundary tests.\n125: \n126: ## References\n127: - `measure/archive/audit_log_infrastructure_20260603/` (the table + helpers this builds on)\n128: - `packages/db/src/schema/audit.ts`, `packages/auth/src/audit.ts` (committed `87b2432`)\n129: - `packages/auth` permission `audit:read:all` (commit `5eb0171`)\n130: - `lib/platform/session-cleanup.ts` (periodic-job template)\n131: - `measure/tracks/rate_limiter_v2_20260603/` (Postgres-backed cleanup + advisory-lock pattern)\n132: - AGENTS.md §9 (Observability) + §5 (Database / tenancy)\n\n(End of file - total 132 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Specification: Audit Log Retention + DSAR Bulk Export\n\n## Overview\n\nTwo compliance capabilities that sit directly on top of the append-only `audit_events`\ntable delivered by `audit_log_infrastructure_20260603`:\n\n1. **Retention** — a 7-year (FERPA) retention window with a periodic, idempotent cleanup\n   job that deletes `audit_events` rows older than the window. Append-only `REVOKE\n   UPDATE, DELETE` means the cleanup job must run as a privileged role; the deletion path\n   is the *only* sanctioned mutation and is itself audited.\n2. **DSAR bulk export** — a GDPR/FERPA Data Subject Access Request endpoint that, given a\n   subject (user id or email), gathers all audit events and profile/activity records for\n   that subject into a single downloadable archive (JSON + a human-readable manifest),\n   ADMIN-only and tenant-scoped.\n\n## Problem\n\nDistrict procurement and GDPR/FERPA compliance require both (a) a defensible data\nlifecycle (data is not kept forever) and (b) the ability to answer \"what do you hold","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/reading-advantage-monorepo/measure/tracks/audit_log_retention_dsar_20260605/spec.md","text":"# Specification: Audit Log Retention + DSAR Bulk Export\n\n## Overview\n\nTwo compliance capabilities that sit directly on top of the append-only `audit_events`\ntable delivered by `audit_log_infrastructure_20260603`:\n\n1. **Retention** — a 7-year (FERPA) retention window with a periodic, idempotent cleanup\n   job that deletes `audit_events` rows older than the window. Append-only `REVOKE\n   UPDATE, DELETE` means the cleanup job must run as a privileged role; the deletion path\n   is the *only* sanctioned mutation and is itself audited.\n2. **DSAR bulk export** — a GDPR/FERPA Data Subject Access Request endpoint that, given a\n   subject (user id or email), gathers all audit events and profile/activity records for\n   that subject into a single downloadable archive (JSON + a human-readable manifest),\n   ADMIN-only and tenant-scoped.\n\n## Problem\n\nDistrict procurement and GDPR/FERPA compliance require both (a) a defensible data\nlifecycle (data is not kept forever) and (b) the ability to answer \"what do you hold\nabout this person, and prove it.\" The audit-log track established the *write* side; this\ntrack establishes the *lifecycle* and *read-out* sides. Without retention, `audit_events`\ngrows unbounded and violates data-minimization principles. Without DSAR export, the\norganization cannot satisfy a subject access request within the statutory window.\n\n## Why\n\n- **FERPA**: education records have a defined retention obligation; 7 years is the policy\n  chosen for this monorepo (configurable via env).\n- **GDPR Art. 15 (right of access) + Art. 17 (right to erasure)**: a subject can request\n  a copy of their data and, separately, deletion. This track delivers Art. 15 (access)\n  and the retention half of Art. 17 (time-bounded deletion); subject-initiated erasure is\n  out of scope (see below).\n- Builds entirely on already-committed infrastructure (`audit_events`,\n  `recordAuditEvent`, the ADMIN-only `/api/admin/audit-events` pattern).\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### FR-1: Retention Policy Configuration\n- Add `AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS` to the validated env surface (default `2557` ≈ 7 years).\n- Add a `.refine` rule: must be a positive integer ≥ 365 (refuse footgun short windows).\n- Document the policy in `packages/auth/README.md` and a new\n  `docs/compliance/retention.md`.\n\n### FR-2: Privileged Cleanup Path\n- Because `audit_events` has `REVOKE UPDATE, DELETE` for the app role, deletion must run\n  under a dedicated migration/maintenance role (the same role that owns DDL).\n- Add `packages/auth/src/audit-retention.ts` exporting\n  `purgeExpiredAuditEvents(now = new Date()): Promise<{ deleted: number }>` that issues a\n  batched `DELETE ... WHERE created_at < now() - interval` with `LIMIT 5000` per batch,\n  looping until no rows remain, using a direct (non-pooled, privileged) connection.\n- The purge run itself records an `audit:retention_purge` event (count, window, actor =\n  `system`) **after** the batch completes, via `recordAuditEvent`.\n\n### FR-3: Periodic Cleanup Job\n- Add a scheduler entry (mirror `lib/platform/session-cleanup.ts`) that runs\n  `purgeExpiredAuditEvents` daily at a low-traffic hour.\n- Idempotent; safe to run concurrently (advisory lock via `pg_try_advisory_lock` so two\n  replicas don't double-run).\n\n### FR-4: DSAR Export Domain Function\n- Add `packages/domain/src/audit/dsar.ts` (or extend `packages/domain/src/audit/`)\n  exporting `exportSubjectData(tenant, subjectRef): Promise<DsarBundle>` where\n  `subjectRef = { userId } | { email }`.\n- `DsarBundle` collects: the user profile, all `audit_events` where the subject is actor\n  or target, and the subject's activity/progress rows (scoped to the science-advantage\n  domain modules already migrated). Tenant-scoped via `createTenantDB`.\n- Guarded by `assertCan(actor, 'audit:read:all')` (the permission added in commit\n  `5eb0171`) plus an explicit `dsar:export` permission key (add to `packages/auth`).\n\n### FR-5: DSAR Export Endpoint\n- Add `GET /api/admin/dsar/export?userId=...` (or `?email=...`), ADMIN-only, Zod-validated\n  query (exactly one of `userId`/`email`).\n- Returns `application/zip` (or `application/json` with `?format=json`) containing\n  `manifest.md` (human-readable summary: who, when, what categories, counts) +\n  `audit-events.json` + `profile.json` + `activity.json`.\n- The export action is itself audited as `dsar:export` (actor = requesting admin,\n  target = subject).\n\n### FR-6: Rate + Size Guards\n- DSAR export is bounded: stream/paginate `audit_events` (do not load all rows into\n  memory); cap a single export at a configurable row ceiling and return `413` with a\n  guidance message if exceeded (operator can raise the ceiling).\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n- The cleanup job must never delete rows inside the retention window (off-by-one and\n  timezone correctness covered by tests at the boundary).\n- Export must be tenant-isolated: an admin in school A cannot export a subject in school B.\n- `pnpm turbo run {test,build,check-types} --filter=@reading-advantage/auth\n  --filter=@reading-advantage/domain --filter=science-advantage` exits 0.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n1. `AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS` is validated env (default 2557; `.refine` ≥ 365).\n2. `purgeExpiredAuditEvents` deletes only rows older than the window, in batches, under a\n   privileged connection, and records an `audit:retention_purge` event.\n3. Daily scheduled job runs the purge under an advisory lock.\n4. `exportSubjectData(tenant, subjectRef)` returns a tenant-scoped bundle gated by\n   `assertCan(... 'dsar:export')`.\n5. `GET /api/admin/dsar/export` returns a zip/JSON archive; ADMIN-only; Zod-validated.\n6. The export action is audited as `dsar:export`.\n7. Tests: boundary retention (row at window-1 day kept, window+1 day purged); advisory\n   lock prevents concurrent double-run; cross-tenant export denied; export-too-large\n   returns 413; export bundle round-trips (manifest counts == file counts).\n8. Quality gates green (test/build/check-types) for the four filtered packages/app.\n\n## Out of Scope\n- **Subject-initiated erasure** (GDPR Art. 17 \"right to be forgotten\" on demand) — audit\n  events are append-only and legally retained; erasure of *profile* data is a separate\n  track with its own legal-hold rules.\n- **Real-time audit-event streaming** to a SIEM — soft-depends on\n  `observability_stack_20260603`; this track is batch-only.\n- Retention for tables other than `audit_events` (sessions, login_attempts have their own\n  cleanup) — separate, already-tracked.\n- A UI for DSAR export — endpoint only; admin console wiring is a follow-up.\n\n## Constraints & Risks\n- **Risk: running DELETE against an append-only table.** Mitigation: the privileged\n  connection is the *only* path; it is exercised exclusively by the purge function, which\n  is itself audited. Document the role separation.\n- **Risk: DSAR export is a PII egress point.** Mitigation: ADMIN-only, tenant-scoped,\n  audited, size-capped, and uses the same `safeMetadata` redaction posture for any nested\n  metadata that should not leave the system.\n- **Risk: timezone/off-by-one in retention boundary.** Mitigation: store + compare in UTC\n  (`withTimezone: true`); explicit boundary tests.\n\n## References\n- `measure/archive/audit_log_infrastructure_20260603/` (the table + helpers this builds on)\n- `packages/db/src/schema/audit.ts`, `packages/auth/src/audit.ts` (committed `87b2432`)\n- `packages/auth` permission `audit:read:all` (commit `5eb0171`)\n- `lib/platform/session-cleanup.ts` (periodic-job template)\n- `measure/tracks/rate_limiter_v2_20260603/` (Postgres-backed cleanup + advisory-lock pattern)\n- AGENTS.md §9 (Observability) + §5 (Database / tenancy)","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":132,"totalLines":132,"truncated":false}},"title":"measure/tracks/audit_log_retention_dsar_20260605/spec.md","time":{"start":1780723395867,"end":1780723395955}},"id":"prt_e9b62a655001QNMb1Vhoi7he8z","sessionID":"ses_1649db034ffe5PYzRZZZhfwsIg","messageID":"msg_e9b6292e9001Zr01gInx7VdxvR"}}
